      {
        "position": 2,
        "title": "My dogs hate it, but it gets the job done",
        "text": "The picture I've included is without me doing any adjustments to the muzzle strapping.We've never really muzzled our pups before, but I've been trying to get ones that we can have on hand for 2 reasons. 1) our 1 pup is terrified of having his nails cut to the point where our vet wouldn't do it without some light sedation and when we've done it at home it took copious amounts of drugs and he still battled us for HOURS and we basically just wore him out. But we didn't have much choice because the whole reason he got that way was from his thumb nail getting too long and he ripped it off by mistake and since then is terrified of things messing with his nails. So when we try to trim nails he will actually snap at us and nip at us! But we also can't just fork out to get him sedated every time he needs TWO nails trimmed (literally all of their other nails stay naturally filed down from running around on our patio).The other reason I wanted to have some on hand and liked getting this as a pair is that when we have those really bad cicada brood years.... we learned that our pups LOVE the little tasty juicy cicadas coming up out of the ground before they dry out and get that crispy hard exoskeleton hardened. GROSS. They will eat them to the point of puking and having endless diarrhea. And that's NOT a fun experience for anyone. I'm not sure how well these will stop them from slurping up bugs since the snout at the end is open, but I'm down to give it a try next time there's a big brood hatch.The strap around the back of the head is adjustable and on top of that there is even a little locking mechanism on the clasp. The wrap part around the muzzle has dual velcro straps so that you can adjust that part too for various snout shapes and circumferences to get the best fit for your pup. The mesh feels pretty durable while also allowing for breathability, so I'm pretty pleased with the quality so far! We're going to have to probably just periodically put these on our pups to train them to be more comfortable wearing them. But it DOES get the job done for stopping any sort of biting.",
